    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "CISA新增CVE-2026-9082：Drupal核心SQL注入漏洞進入已知利用漏洞清單",
    summary: "美國網路安全局（CISA）宣布將一個新的漏洞，CVE-2026-9082，加入其「已知利用漏洞清單」（Known Exploited Vulnerabilities, KEV Catalog）。此漏洞為Drupal核心的SQL注入漏洞，已被證實存在活躍的攻擊利用證據，對聯邦企業網路構成重大風險。該清單的設立源於《強制性營運指令》（BOD 22-01），要求聯邦民事行政部門（FCEB）必須在指定期限內修復這些已知漏洞，以保護其網路免受活躍威脅。雖然指令僅適用於FCEB機構，但CISA強烈敦促所有組織將修補KEV清單中的漏洞，作為其漏洞管理流程的優先事項，以降低整體網路暴露風險。建議所有使用Drupal系統的組織，應立即評估並修補此類已知的、且已被利用的漏洞。",
    tags: ["CISA", "KEV Catalog", "CVE-2026-9082", "Drupal", "SQL Injection", "漏洞管理"],
    title_en: "CISA Adds CVE-2026-9082: Drupal Core SQL Injection Vulnerability Enters Known Exploited Vulnerabilities List",
    summary_en: "The U.S. Cybersecurity and Infrastructure Security Agency (CISA) announced the addition of a new vulnerability, CVE-2026-9082, to its Known Exploited Vulnerabilities (KEV) Catalog. This vulnerability is a SQL injection flaw in the Drupal core, for which active exploitation evidence has been confirmed, posing a significant risk to federal enterprise networks. The establishment of this catalog stems from the Mandatory Operational Directive (BOD 22-01), which requires Federal Civilian Executive Branch (FCEB) agencies to remediate these known vulnerabilities within a specified timeframe to protect their networks from active threats. Although the directive only applies to FCEB agencies, CISA strongly urges all organizations to prioritize patching vulnerabilities listed in the KEV catalog as part of their vulnerability management process to reduce overall network exposure risk. Organizations using Drupal systems are advised to immediately assess and patch such known, exploited vulnerabilities.",
    tags_en: ["CISA", "KEV Catalog", "CVE-2026-9082", "Drupal", "SQL Injection", "漏洞管理"],
    sources: [
      { name: "CISA Advisories", url: "https://cisa.gov/news-events/alerts/2026/05/22/cisa-adds-one-known-exploited-vulnerability-catalog", lang: "EN" }
    ]
