    id: "20260522-007",
    trackers: ["security"],
    category: "漏洞與威脅情報",
    title: "網路邊緣設備至內部 Linux 伺服器，再經由 Confluence 應用程式進行多階段入侵分析",
    summary: "本次事件展示了現代入侵的趨勢：攻擊者利用網路邊緣設備（如防火牆、VPN 閘道）的漏洞作為初始立足點，進而透過信任關係進行橫向移動。攻擊鏈從一台 F5 BIG-IP 負載平衡器（版本 15.1.201000，已過時）開始，取得 SSH 存取權限進入內部 Linux 主機。隨後，攻擊者進行了廣泛的內網掃描和偵察，並發現了存在未修補漏洞的 Atlassian Confluence 伺服器。攻擊者利用這些漏洞執行遠端程式碼，取得憑證。最後，攻擊者利用這些憑證，嘗試對 Active Directory 進行身份驗證攻擊，顯示了攻擊鏈跨越了網路基礎設施、Linux 端點、SaaS 平台和身份系統的複雜性。組織應將邊緣設備、非 Windows 系統和雲端身份視為安全關鍵資產，並優先進行攻擊路徑分析。",
    tags: ["F5 BIG-IP", "Confluence", "Linux", "邊緣設備", "橫向移動", "身份系統"],
    title_en: "Multi-stage intrusion analysis from network edge device to internal Linux server, via Confluence application",
    summary_en: "This incident demonstrates a trend in modern intrusions: attackers utilize vulnerabilities in network edge devices (such as firewalls or VPN gateways) as initial footholds, subsequently performing lateral movement through trusted relationships. The attack chain began with an outdated F5 BIG-IP load balancer (version 15.1.201000), which allowed the attacker to gain SSH access to an internal Linux host. Subsequently, the attacker conducted extensive internal network scanning and reconnaissance, discovering an Atlassian Confluence server with unpatched vulnerabilities. The attacker exploited these vulnerabilities to execute remote code, obtaining credentials. Finally, the attacker used these credentials to attempt an Active Directory authentication attack, highlighting the complexity of the attack chain spanning network infrastructure, Linux endpoints, SaaS platforms, and identity systems. Organizations should treat edge devices, non-Windows systems, and cloud identity as critical security assets and prioritize attack path analysis.",
    tags_en: ["F5 BIG-IP", "Confluence", "Linux", "Edge Device", "Lateral Movement", "Identity System"],
    sources: [
      { name: "Microsoft Security Blog", url: "https://microsoft.com/en-us/security/blog/2026/05/22/from-edge-appliance-to-enterprise-compromise-multi-stage-linux-intrusion-via-f5-and-confluence", lang: "EN" }
    ]
